//Function Overloading

Function overloading means having multiple functions with the same name but different parameters in the same class/scope.

Example:

class Calculator {
public:
    int add(int a, int b) {
        return a + b;
    }

    int add(int a, int b, int c) {
        return a + b + c;
    }
};

Now:

Calculator c;

c.add(2, 3);       // calls first function
c.add(2, 3, 4);    // calls second function

The compiler knows which function to call based on the number/type of arguments.

Important

Changing only the return type is NOT function overloading.

❌ Not valid:

int add(int a, int b);
double add(int a, int b);
Simple definition

Function overloading = same function name, different parameter list.

It is an example of compile-time polymorphism.